# L §5.18: "A deflator is written in the ask, x * idx[base] / idx[d]: a lens applied only when a question is asked"
# (writer 8: real() is gone). 5 000.00 × 100 / 125 = 4 000.00. The run starts in 2020, so 2020 is a key of years
# (L §4.1). money × num is num CUR (L §3.2), and the division keeps it so: a num PLN, not money.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2020-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input cpi[y in years]: num
input wage: money PLN

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  cpi[2020] = 100
  cpi[2026] = 125
  wage = 5 000.00 PLN

ask q1: wage * cpi[2020] / cpi[2026]
=== expect
q1: 4 000 PLN
  cut 2026-12-31
